/E ( Life in Barangay Antonio Luna slowly began to rebuild. Neighbors helped each other clean the streets, children played again under the bright morning sun, and laughter slowly replaced the cries of fear. The same storm that destroyed their homes built something far stronger unity, compassion, and faith.Typhoon Tino may have tested their strength, but it also revealed their hearts. Jessa and her neighbors learned that the greatest power of all is not found in walls or roofs, but in the love that keeps people standing even when everything else has fallen.)
