/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Before the first light of dawn touches Tagbongabong, RTR, Agusan del Norte, Ritchel Seballo is already on her feet. Her worn-out sleepers slap softly against the dusty road, marking the start of a journey that many would consider impossible for a young girl, walking kilometers through muddy roads just to reach Calamba National High School.The road is long and unrelenting. Some days, the sun beats down mercilessly, leaving her feet blistered and her skin raw. Other days, sudden tropical rain drenches her, soaking her uniform and weighing down her backpack. Yet Ritchel does not complain. Each step is fueled by a single goal: education and the hope of a brighter future)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
