397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T ( Rice farmers in the Philippines face a persistent enemy in the rice field rat \(Rattus argentiventer\). These rodents destroy seedlings, damage panicles, and burrow into dikes, leading to significant yield losses. Traditional control methods such as chemical rodenticides, electrified barriers, and manual hunting can reduce rat populations but often harm the environment, require heavy labor, or pose safety risks.  Seeking a safer solution, student-researchers from Calamba National High School designed the Rice Field Rat Control Flashing LED Light Device, a solar-powered innovation that uses blue flashing lights to disperse rats without toxic chemicals. Research shows that rats avoid high light intensity and experience stress under flickering lights. According to Brudzynski \(2023\), rats demonstrate anxiety-like behaviors in brightly lit areas, while Shang \(2021\) found that prolonged LED exposure can damage their retinas, discouraging return to those locations.)
/E ( Rice farmers in the Philippines face a persistent enemy in the rice field rat \(Rattus argentiventer\). These rodents destroy seedlings, damage panicles, and burrow into dikes, leading to significant yield losses. Traditional control methods such as chemical rodenticides, electrified barriers, and manual hunting can reduce rat populations but often harm the environment, require heavy labor, or pose safety risks.  Seeking a safer solution, student-researchers from Calamba National High School designed the Rice Field Rat Control Flashing LED Light Device, a solar-powered innovation that uses blue flashing lights to disperse rats without toxic chemicals. Research shows that rats avoid high light intensity and experience stress under flickering lights. According to Brudzynski \(2023\), rats demonstrate anxiety-like behaviors in brightly lit areas, while Shang \(2021\) found that prolonged LED exposure can damage their retinas, discouraging return to those locations.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
