402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The Philippines has already implemented few major flood control projects, such as the Pasig-Marikina River Channel Improvement Project and the Taguig-Pateros Flood Control System. Meanwhile, local governments in provinces like Agusan del Norte and Pampanga are constructing small-scale flood barriers and rainwater catchment areas suited to their local geography. However, infrastructure alone is not enough. Community awareness and participation are equally important. Residents should practice proper waste disposal, as clogged canals and drainage systems often worsen flooding. Schools and barangays must also educate citizens about flood preparedness and emergency response. As climate change intensifies, stronger typhoons and heavier rainfall are expected in the coming years. Flood control projects, grounded in science, engineering, and cooperation within communities, offer our strongest protection. With collective effort, the Philippines can rise above the waters, protecting both its people and its future.)
/E (The Philippines has already implemented few major flood control projects, such as the Pasig-Marikina River Channel Improvement Project and the Taguig-Pateros Flood Control System. Meanwhile, local governments in provinces like Agusan del Norte and Pampanga are constructing small-scale flood barriers and rainwater catchment areas suited to their local geography. However, infrastructure alone is not enough. Community awareness and participation are equally important. Residents should practice proper waste disposal, as clogged canals and drainage systems often worsen flooding. Schools and barangays must also educate citizens about flood preparedness and emergency response. As climate change intensifies, stronger typhoons and heavier rainfall are expected in the coming years. Flood control projects, grounded in science, engineering, and cooperation within communities, offer our strongest protection. With collective effort, the Philippines can rise above the waters, protecting both its people and its future.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [17 18 19]
>>
